---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii3_38",
  "series": "Band II 3 (1695 - 1700)",
  "seq": 38,
  "text": "<p> [[105.1]] <b>38. LEIBNIZ AN MENTET KETTWIG</p>\n<p> [[105.2]] Hannover, 7. (17.) November 1695. [35.44.]</b></p>\n\n<p> [[105.18]] [<i>l</i>] </p>\n<p> [[105.19]] Ex responsione.\n [[105.20]] Nobilissimo et Consultissimo Viro Dn. Menteto Kettwigio Icto doctissimo.\n [[105.21]] Godefridus Guilielmus Leibnitius. S. P. D. </p>\n<p> [[105.22]] Pro munere pereleganti gratias debitas reddo, et illis applaudo libens qui ad constituendam\n[[105.23]] solidiorem jurisprudentiam ut te placere video diligentiam doctrinamque conferunt. Placet in\n[[105.24]] tuis vel ipsa scribendi forma, qua sententiam tueris, salvo cultu qui excellenti adversario\n[[105.25]] debebatur. De rebus ipsis tecum in eo sentio, quod literis etiam tuis attingis, magno acumine\n[[105.26]] Hobbium scripsisse de civili philosophia. Addo ne in illis quidem spernendum videri ubi\n[[105.27]] dissentire necesse est. Magnorum certe virorum etiam erratis solemus doceri. Itaque Hermannum\n[[106.1]] Conringium alicubi insanientem Hobbii sapientiam dicere miratus sum, eo magis quod alioqui\n[[106.2]] censorem novis quoque Scriptoribus non iniquum deprehenderim. Quid ego de doctrina Hobbiana\n[[106.3]] sentiam, tum ex <i>Codicis diplomatici</i> praefatione, tum ex libello quem <i>Novae juris\n[[106.4]] methodi</i> titulo adolescens scripseram, tum vero maxime ex nonnullis intelligi potest quibus\n[[106.5]] nomen meum non praescripsi. Sed nolo Te tenere diutius, non defuturus occasioni, si qua sese\n[[106.6]] offerat, qua testari possim, quantum illis deberi judicem, qui literis laborantibus opem ferre\n[[106.7]] possunt. Vale. Dabam Hannoverae VI. Novembr. MDCVC. <Fn><i>Auf der Folgeseite, Bl. 2 r^#'o, von Leibniz' Hand</i>: In ejus naturali philosophia probare [<i>bricht ab</i>]</Fn> </p>\n<p> [[106.8]] [<i>L</i>] </p>\n<p> [[106.9]] Nobilissimo et Consultissimo Viro Domino Menteto Kettwigio\n [[106.10]] Godefridus Guilielmus Leibnitius S. P. D. </p>\n<p> [[106.11]] Pro munere pereleganti gratias debitas reddo, et illis applaudo libens, qui constituendae\n[[106.12]] solidiori jurisprudentiae doctrinam diligentiamque conferunt, quod Tibi propositum video.\n[[106.13]] Placet in his quae mittis vel ipsa scribendi forma qua sententiam tueris salvo cultu qui\n[[106.14]] excellenti adversario debebatur. </p>\n<p> [[106.15]] De rebus ipsis in eo tecum sentio, quod literis etiam tuis attingis, magno acumine\n[[106.16]] Hobbium scripsisse qui et mihi est inde a puero lectus. Addo ne in illis quidem spernendum\n[[106.17]] videri ubi dissentire necesse est. Geometrica tamen excipio, in quibus tantopere errare potuisse\n[[106.18]] virum ingeniosissimum, et in ea ipsa scientia praeclare versatum inter singularia mentis humanae\n[[106.19]] recenseo, quorum rationem reddere difficile est. Quae de corporis natura scripsit plurimum\n[[106.20]] habent boni. Sed dum nil nisi corpus admittit in rebus, philosophiam suam caetera egregiam\n[[106.21]] misere corrupit. </p>\n<p> [[106.22]] De rebus civilibus, principiisque justi vera multa et praeclara, sed non sufficientia dixit.\n[[106.23]] Agnosco homines mutuo metu et necessitate ad colendam societatem constituendamque\n[[107.1]] potestatem societatis custodem cogi; sed praeter metum amor, praeter miseriae fugam, felicitatis\n[[107.2]] illecebra accessit, quae mutuis inprimis auxiliis constat. Eaque ipsa in <i>Codicis diplomatici</i>\n[[107.3]] praefatione distinxi. Ab Amore igitur juris fontes repeto, sed qui sit dignus sapiente; amor\n[[107.4]] autem tendit ad felicitatem, in quo inest vitare miseriam, et dare operam, ne nobis exitiosa sit\n[[107.5]] cura alieni boni. Itaque quod in Hobbianis principiis rectum inest, altioribus illis continetur, non\n[[107.6]] vicissim. </p>\n<p> [[107.7]] Sed nec Hobbiana de summa potestate decreta certis demonstrationibus colliguntur aut\n[[107.8]] rebus humanis congruunt. Si illum audimus, quisquis potestatem summam habet, omnimodam\n[[107.9]] habet, nec possumus partiri jura regnandi; usque adeo ut in Regis arbitrio sit etiam de successore\n[[107.10]] constituere. Quod tamen ne in ipsa quidem Gallia feretur. Argumenta quibus haec probare\n[[107.11]] instituit, satis virium non habent. Fateor incommoda metui posse dissensu eorum, quibus\n[[107.12]] creditae sunt diversae partes reipublicae. Sed non omne quod incommoda trahit intolerabile aut\n[[107.13]] vitabile est. Quin potius districtas illas sententias Hobbianas, et Metaphysicam alieno loco\n[[107.14]] exercitam obtrudere mentibus humanis multo plus difficultatis haberet. Neque facile gentem\n[[107.15]] reperias, cui non circa gubernationis formam alia omnia placuisse constet. Illud tamen et probo\n[[107.16]] et tueor possessori supremae potestatis resistendum non esse. Quanquam non sit haec regula\n[[107.17]] tam abscissae aut Mathematicae veritatis ut exceptionem nullam ferat, non magis quam aliae\n[[108.1]] pleraeque civiles sententiae. Non possunt demonstrari positiones juris et aequi, nisi ex consideratione\n[[108.2]] boni, cujus cessantis inest illis exceptio, quemadmodum apud IC^#'t^#'o^#'s regulis exceptiones\n[[108.3]] saepe insunt ipso jure. Itaque si manifeste in publicum exitium feratur, et veluti furat qui\n[[108.4]] rebus praeest, Grotio assentior. Et cum justitia (mea definitione) sit caritas sapientis, justum\n[[108.5]] non puto, quod absurdum est, quale fuerit, perdere Rempublicam, ut formam regnandi tueamur,\n[[108.6]] quae tamen ideo reperta est, ne pereat Respublica. Ut illud Poetae non longe absit:\n [[108.7]] <i>Hic rogo non furor est ne moriare mori?</i>\n [[108.8]] Quae talia sunt, ut nec Te dissentire arbitrer. Et Hobbium longius etiam facultatem resistendi\n[[108.9]] extendere scio, quam a me probetur. Nam etiam reus capitis, etiam non innocens, jus apud\n[[108.10]] ipsum habet, omnia pessundandi, ut sit salvus. Quod et ego admitterem, si vita nostra hac vita\n[[108.11]] finiretur. </p>\n<p> [[108.12]] Sed nescio quomodo praeter institutum sese diffudit Epistola. Vale vir clarissime, et hoc\n[[108.13]] Tibi persuade nunquam me occasioni defuturum, qua Tibi testari possim, quantum illis deberi\n[[108.14]] judicem, qui recta studia ornare possunt. Dabam Hanoverae 7 Novemb. 1695. </p></p>\n",
  "number": "38.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN MENTET KETTWIG",
  "date": "Hannover, 7. (17.) November 1695. [35.44.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:38. LEIBNIZ AN MENTET KETTWIG Hannover, 7. (17.) November 1695. [35.44.] [l] Ex responsione. Nobilissimo et Consultissimo Viro Dn. Menteto Kettwigio Icto doctissimo. Godefridus Guilielmus Leibnitius. S. P. D. Pro munere pereleganti gratias debitas reddo, et illis applaudo libens qui ad constituendam...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>